The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```java
@Test
public void testNonSecureFunctionality() {
    // Non-secure test code
}

@Test
public void testSecureFunctionality() {
    // Secure test code that requires authentication
}
```
Reason:
The tests for secure and non-secure functionalities were not properly isolated, causing authentication conflicts when both types of tests were executed in the same JVM. This led to failures in the secure tests due to interference from the non-secure tests.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
@Category(SecureTests.class)
public class SecureTestSuite {
    // Secure tests run in a dedicated JVM
}

@Category(NonSecureTests.class)
public class NonSecureTestSuite {
    // Non-secure tests run in a separate JVM
}
```
Reason:
By separating the secure and non-secure tests into their own modules and running them in dedicated JVMs, the authentication conflicts are eliminated, allowing each test suite to operate independently without interference.

